Naming and visual identity
--------------------------
The application is called **Spark Game Launcher**. The name deliberately
contains no NVIDIA trademark -- no "DGX", "RTX", "NVIDIA", "CUDA", "GeForce" or
"Blackwell" -- and the word "Spark" is used descriptively, of the class of
machine the software targets.

The application deliberately does NOT imitate NVIDIA's visual identity:

  * It uses none of NVIDIA's logos, wordmarks, icons or product imagery.
  * It uses NO NVIDIA green. The colour appears nowhere in the application.
  * Its palette is gold plus arcade neon (blue, purple, pink), chosen to read as
    a gaming utility rather than as a vendor product.

This is a deliberate design decision, recorded because it is the point:
NVIDIA's brand-usage guidance asks third parties not to mimic NVIDIA's branding
and visual style. This project follows that, in substance rather than in a
footnote.

If NVIDIA, HP, Valve or Canonical would like anything here changed or removed,
open an issue -- it will be addressed promptly and in good faith.
